n//                         }\n//                     }\n//                     if (found == false)\n//                         variables.push(variable);\n//                 }\n//             }\n//         }\n//     }\n//\n//     ui.resCovSupplier.setValue(context.valuesToItems(variables, FormatDef.variable));\n// };\n//\n// module.exports = events;\n//\n//\n//\n// }\n\n\n\n\n//    module.exports = {\n//\n//        // event handlers and functions are defined here\n//\n//        // this is an example of an event handler\n//        view_loaded: function(ui, event) {\n//            // do something\n//        },\n//\n//        // this is another example of an event handler\n//        ttestType_changed: function(ui, event) {\n//            let value = this.calculateValue();\n//            // do something\n//        },\n//\n//        // this is an example of an auxiliary function\n//        calculateValue: function() {\n//            // do something\n//        }\n//\n//       ui.view.model.options.beginEdit();\n//       ui.figWidth.setValue(400);\n//       ui.figHeight.setValue(300);\n//       ui.view.model.options.endEdit();\n//\n//    };\n\n},{}],2:[function(require,module,exports){\n\n// This file is an automatically generated and should not be edited\n\n'use strict';\n\nconst options = [{\"name\":\"data\",\"type\":\"Data\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"A data.frame.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"row_vars\",\"title\":\"<b>row_vars = <i>(row variables)</i></b>\",\"type\":\"Variables\",\"permitted\":[\"numeric\",\"factor\"],\"default\":null,\"suggested\":[\"nominal\",\"ordinal\"],\"description\":{\"R\":\"The row variable, which will be printed with one level per line. If numeric, it will be converted to factor. If several row variables are provided, it's not possible to add any tab_vars.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"col_vars\",\"title\":\"<b>col_vars = <i>(column variables)</i></b>\",\"type\":\"Variables\",\"suggested\":[\"nominal\",\"ordinal\",\"continuous\"],\"permitted\":[\"numeric\",\"factor\"],\"default\":null,\"description\":{\"R\":\"One column is printed for each level of each column variable. For numeric variables means are calculated, in a single column.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"tab_vars\",\"title\":\"<b>tab_vars = <i>(subtables variables)</i></b>\",\"type\":\"Variables\",\"suggested\":[\"nominal\",\"ordinal\"],\"permitted\":[\"factor\"],\"default\":null,\"description\":{\"R\":\"One subtable is made for each combination of levels of the tab variables. All tab variables are converted to factor. Leave empty to make a simple table. Not used when there are several row_vars.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"wt\",\"title\":\"<b>wt = <i>(weights)</i></b>\",\"type\":\"Variable\",\"suggested\":[\"continuous\"],\"permitted\":[\"numeric\"],\"default\":null,\"description\":{\"R\":\"A weight variable, of class numeric. Leave empty for unweighted results.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"pct\",\"title\":\"pct = (Percentages)\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"no (counts)\",\"name\":\"no\"},{\"title\":\"row\",\"name\":\"row\"},{\"title\":\"col (column)\",\"name\":\"col\"},{\"title\":\"all\",\"name\":\"all\"},{\"title\":\"all_tabs\",\"name\":\"all_tabs\"}],\"default\":\"no\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"The type of percentages to calculate :\\n \\\\itemize{\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"row\\\"}: row percentages.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"col\\\"}: column percentages.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"all\\\"}: frequencies for each subtable/group, if there is \\\\code{tab_vars}.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"all_tabs\\\"}: frequencies for the whole (set of) table(s).\\n }\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"color\",\"title\":\"color = (Color)\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"no\",\"name\":\"no\"},{\"title\":\"diff <i>(differences from total, or reference cell)</i>\",\"name\":\"diff\"},{\"title\":\"diff_ci <i>(differences, only if significant)</i>\",\"name\":\"diff_ci\"},{\"title\":\"after_ci <i>(diff, after substracting margin of error)</i>\",\"name\":\"after_ci\"},{\"title\":\"contrib <i>(relative contribution to variance)</i>\",\"name\":\"contrib\"},{\"title\":\"OR <i>(odds ratios or relative risks ratios)</i>\",\"name\":\"OR\"}],\"default\":\"no\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"The type of colors to print, as a single string. Vectorised over `row_vars`.\\n \\\\itemize{\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"no\\\"}: by default, no colors are printed.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"diff\\\"}: color percentages and means based on cells differences from\\n   totals (or from first cells when \\\\code{ref = \\\"first\\\"}).\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"diff_ci\\\"}: color pct and means based on cells differences from totals\\n   or first cells, removing coloring when the confidence interval of this difference\\n   is higher than the difference itself.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"after_ci\\\"}: idem, but cut off the confidence interval from the\\n   difference first.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"contrib\\\"}: color cells based on their contribution to variance\\n   (except mean columns, from numeric variables).\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"OR\\\"}: for `pct == \\\"col\\\"` or `pct == \\\"row\\\"`,\\n   color based on odds ratios (or relative risks ratios)\\n }\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"chi2\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bool\",\"default\":false,\"description\":{\"R\":\"Set to \\\\code{TRUE} to make a Chi2 and add summary stats. Also useful to color cells based on their contribution to variance.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"OR\",\"title\":\"OR\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"no\",\"name\":\"no\"},{\"title\":\"OR\",\"name\":\"OR\"},{\"title\":\"OR_pct\",\"name\":\"OR_pct\"}],\"default\":\"no\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"With `pct = \\\"row\\\"` or `pct = \\\"col\\\"`, calculate and print odds ratios\\n (for binary variables) or relative risks ratios (for variables with 3 levels\\n or more).\\n\\\\itemize{\\n \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"no\\\"}: by default, no OR are calculated.\\n \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"OR\\\"}: print OR (instead of percentages).\\n \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"OR_pct\\\"}: print OR, with percentages in bracket.\\n}\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"na\",\"title\":\"na = <i>(missing values)</i>\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"keep\",\"name\":\"keep\"},{\"title\":\"drop <i>(for each col_var)</i>\",\"name\":\"drop\"},{\"title\":\"drop_all <i>(for all col_vars)</i>\",\"name\":\"drop_all\"}],\"default\":\"keep\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"The policy to adopt with missing values. It must be a single string.\\n \\\\itemize{\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{na = \\\"keep\\\"}: by default, prints \\\\code{NA}'s as explicit \\\\code{\\\"NA\\\"} level.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{na = \\\"drop\\\"}: removes \\\\code{NA} levels before making each table\\n   (tabs made with different column variables may have a different number of\\n   observations, and won't exactly have the same total columns).\\n   }\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"lvs\",\"title\":\"levels\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"all\",\"name\":\"all\"},{\"title\":\"first\",\"name\":\"first\"},{\"title\":\"auto\",\"name\":\"auto\"}],\"default\":\"all\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"The levels of \\\\code{col_vars} to keep.\\n \\\\itemize{\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"all\\\"}: by default, all levels are kept.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"first\\\"}: only keep the first level of each \\\\code{col_vars}\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"auto\\\"}: keep the first level when `col_var` is only two levels,\\n   keep all levels otherwise.\\n   }\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"other_if_less_than\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Number\",\"min\":0,\"default\":0,\"description\":{\"R\":\"When set to a positive integer, levels with less count than that will be merged into an \\\"Others\\\" level.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"cleannames\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bool\",\"default\":true,\"description\":{\"R\":\"By default, clean levels names, by removing prefix numbers like \\\"1-\\\", and text in parenthesis. Set to `FALSE` to avoid this behaviour.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"ref\",\"title\":\"auto/tot/<i>{row_number}</i>/<i>{row_name}</i>\",\"type\":\"String\",\"default\":\"auto\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"The reference cell to calculate differences and ratios\\n  (used to print \\\\code{colors}) :\\n  \\\\itemize{\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"auto\\\"}: by default, cell difference from the corresponding total\\n   (rows or cols depending on \\\\code{pct = \\\"row\\\"} or \\\\code{pct = \\\"col\\\"}) is\\n   used for `diff` ; cell ratio from the first line (or col) is use for `OR`\\n   (odds ratio/relative risks ratio).\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"tot\\\"}: totals are always used.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"first\\\"}: calculate cell difference or ratio from the first cell\\n of the row or column (useful to color temporal developments).\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{n}: when `ref` is an integer, the nth row (or column) is used for comparison.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"regex\\\"}: when `ref` is a string, it it used as a regular expression,\\n   to match with the names of the rows (or columns). Be precise enough to match only one\\n   column or row, otherwise you get a warning message.\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"no\\\"}: not use ref and not calculate diffs to gain calculation time.\\n }\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"ref2\",\"title\":\"first/tot/<i>{col_number}</i>\",\"type\":\"String\",\"default\":\"first\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"A second reference cell is needed to calculate odds ratios\\n (or relative risks ratios). The first cell of the row or column is used by default.\\n See `ref`  for the full list of possible values.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"comp\",\"title\":\"comp\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"tab <i>(compare in each subtable)</i>\",\"name\":\"tab\"},{\"title\":\"all <i>(compare with the total subtable)</i>\",\"name\":\"all\"}],\"default\":\"tab\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"The comparison level : by subtables/groups, or for the whole table.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"ci\",\"title\":\"ci = <i>(confidence intervals)</i>\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"auto\",\"name\":\"auto\"},{\"title\":\"cell <i>(ci for each cell)</i>\",\"name\":\"cell\"},{\"title\":\"diff <i>(ci on the difference with reference)</i>\",\"name\":\"diff\"}],\"default\":\"auto\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"The type of confidence intervals to calculate, passed to \\\\code{\\\\link{tab_ci}}.\\n    \\\\itemize{\\n     \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"cell\\\"}: absolute confidence intervals of cells percentages.\\n     \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"diff\\\"}: confidence intervals of the difference between a cell and the\\n     relative total cell (or relative first cell when \\\\code{ref = \\\"first\\\"}).\\n     \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"auto\\\"}: \\\\code{ci = \\\"diff\\\"} for means and row/col percentages,\\n     \\\\code{ci = \\\"cell\\\"} for frequencies (\\\"all\\\", \\\"all_tabs\\\").\\n    }\\nBy default, for percentages, with \\\\code{ci = \\\"cell\\\"} Wilson's method is used, and with \\\\code{ci = \\\"diff\\\"} Wald's method along Agresti and Caffo's adjustment. Means use classic method.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"conf_level\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Number\",\"min\":0,\"max\":1,\"default\":0.95,\"description\":{\"R\":\"The confidence level, as a single numeric between 0 and 1. Default to 0.95 (95%).\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"ci_print\",\"title\":\"options('tabxplor.ci_print' = ...)\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"ci <i>(interval display: [inf;sup])</i>\",\"name\":\"ci\"},{\"title\":\"moe <i>(display: pct±margin of error)</i>\",\"name\":\"moe\"}],\"default\":\"ci\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"By default confidence interval are printed with the interval display. Set to \\\"moe\\\" to use pct +- moe instead.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"totaltab\",\"title\":\"totaltab = <i>(add a total table)</i>\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"line\",\"name\":\"line\"},{\"title\":\"table\",\"name\":\"table\"},{\"title\":\"no\",\"name\":\"no\"}],\"default\":\"line\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"The total table, if there are subtables/groups\\n  (i.e. when \\\\code{tab_vars} is provided). Vectorised over `row_vars`.\\n \\\\itemize{\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"line\\\"}: by default, add a general total line (necessary for\\n   calculations with \\\\code{comp = \\\"all\\\"})\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"table\\\"}: add a complete total table\\n  (i.e. \\\\code{row_var} by \\\\code{col_vars} without \\\\code{tab_vars}).\\n   \\\\item \\\\code{\\\"no\\\"}: not to draw any total table.\\n  }\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"wrap_rows\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Number\",\"min\":0,\"default\":35,\"description\":{\"R\":\"By default, rownames are wrapped when larger than 30 characters.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"wrap_cols\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Number\",\"min\":0,\"default\":15,\"description\":{\"R\":\"By default, colnames are wrapped when larger than 12 characters.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"display\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"List\",\"options\":[{\"title\":\"auto\",\"name\":\"auto\"},{\"title\":\"n <i>(unweighted counts)</i>\",\"name\":\"n\"},{\"title\":\"wn <i>(weighted counts)</i>\",\"name\":\"wn\"},{\"title\":\"pct <i>(percentages)</i>\",\"name\":\"pct\"},{\"title\":\"diff <i>(differences from total, or reference cell)</i>\",\"name\":\"diff\"},{\"title\":\"ctr <i>(relative contributions to variance)</i>\",\"name\":\"ctr\"},{\"title\":\"mean <i>(mean, for numeric variables)</i>\",\"name\":\"mean\"},{\"title\":\"var <i>(variance)</i>\",\"name\":\"var\"},{\"title\":\"ci <i>(confidence intervals)</i>\",\"name\":\"ci\"},{\"title\":\"pct_ci <i>(percentages with visible conf. intervals)</i>\",\"name\":\"pct_ci\"},{\"title\":\"mean_ci <i>(means with visible conf. intervals)</i>\",\"name\":\"mean_ci\"},{\"title\":\"OR <i>(odds ratios or relative risks ratios)</i>\",\"name\":\"OR\"},{\"title\":\"OR_pct <i>(odds ratios with visible percentages)</i>\",\"name\":\"OR_pct\"}],\"default\":\"auto\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"The information to display in the table.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"add_n\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bool\",\"default\":true,\"description\":{\"R\":\"For `pct = \\\"row\\\"` or `pct = \\\"col\\\"`, set to `FALSE` not to add another column or row with unweighted counts (`n`).\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"add_pct\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bool\",\"default\":false,\"description\":{\"R\":\"Set to `TRUE` to add a column with the frequencies of the row variable (for `pct = \\\"row\\\"`) or a row with the frequencies of the column variable (for  `pct = \\\"col\\\"`)\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"subtext\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"String\",\"default\":\"\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"A character vector to print rows of legend under the table.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"digits\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Number\",\"min\":0,\"max\":10,\"default\":0,\"description\":{\"R\":\"The number of digits to print, as a single integer, or an integer vector the same length as \\\\code{col_vars}.\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"exportExcel\",\"title\":\"Export Table to Excel\",\"type\":\"Action\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"Press to export the table to Excel.\"}},{\"name\":\"xl_path\",\"type\":\"String\",\"title\":\"\",\"default\":\"S:/Documents\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"\\\"Folder in which to save exported Excel file\\\"\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"xl_filename\",\"type\":\"String\",\"title\":\"\",\"default\":\"Table.xlsx\",\"description\":{\"R\":\"\\\"Name of exported Excel file\\\"\\n\"}},{\"name\":\"xl_replace\",\"title\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bool\",\"default\":false,\"description\":{\"R\":\"\\\"Set to `TRUE` to overwrite existing Excel file.\\\"\\n\"}}];\n\nconst view = function() {\n    \n    this.handlers = require('./jmvtab')\n\n    View.extend({\n        jus: \"3.0\",\n\n        events: [\n\n\t]\n\n    }).call(this);\n}\n\nview.layout = ui.extend({\n\n    label: \"Crosstables\",\n    jus: \"3.0\",\n    type: \"root\",\n    stage: 0, //0 - release, 1 - development, 2 - proposed\n    controls: [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.VariableSupplier,\n\t\t\ttypeName: 'VariableSupplier',\n\t\t\tname: \"variablesupplier\",\n\t\t\tpersistentItems: false,\n\t\t\tstretchFactor: 1,\n\t\t\tcontrols: [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.TargetLayoutBox,\n\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'TargetLayoutBox',\n\t\t\t\t\tlabel: \"<b>row_vars = <i>(row variables)</i></b>\",\n\t\t\t\t\tcontrols: [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.VariablesListBox,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'VariablesListBox',\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tname: \"row_vars\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tisTarget: true\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.TargetLayoutBox,\n\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'TargetLayoutBox',\n\t\t\t\t\tlabel: \"<b>col_vars = <i>(column variables)</i></b>\",\n\t\t\t\t\tcontrols: [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.VariablesListBox,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'VariablesListBox',\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tname: \"col_vars\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tisTarget: true\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.TargetLayoutBox,\n\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'TargetLayoutBox',\n\t\t\t\t\tlabel: \"<b>tab_vars = <i>(subtables variables)</i></b>\",\n\t\t\t\t\tcontrols: [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.VariablesListBox,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'VariablesListBox',\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tname: \"tab_vars\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tisTarget: true\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.TargetLayoutBox,\n\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'TargetLayoutBox',\n\t\t\t\t\tlabel: \"<b>wt = <i>(weights)</i></b>\",\n\t\t\t\t\tcontrols: [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.VariablesListBox,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'VariablesListBox',\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tname: \"wt\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmaxItemCount: 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tisTarget: true\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.CollapseBox,\n\t\t\ttypeName: 'CollapseBox',\n\t\t\tlabel: \"<b>Percentages, colors and Chi2 test </b>\",\n\t\t\tstretchFactor: 1,\n\t\t\tcollapsed: false,\n\t\t\tcontrols: [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.LayoutBox,\n\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'LayoutBox',\n\t\t\t\t\tmargin: \"large\",\n\t\t\t\t\tcontrols: [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttype: DefaultControls.LayoutBox,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttypeName: 'LayoutBox',\n\